    <briefdescription>
<para>Boxed tensor-product kernel from 2nd order (quadratic) B-splines. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The kernel of node <formula id="9">$ A $</formula> with center <formula id="47">$ \boldsymbol{x}_A $</formula> and support radius <formula id="61">$ a $</formula> is the tensor product of one-dimensional 2nd order (quadratic) B-splines <formula id="81">$ w $</formula> in each coordinate direction,   <formula id="82">\[  \phi_A(\boldsymbol{x}) = \prod_{i=1}^{d} w\left( x_i - x_{A,i} \right),
\]</formula> with      <formula id="83">\[  w(r) = \begin{cases} 1 - 2 z^2, &amp; 0 \le z \le \tfrac{1}{2}, \\
                       2 (1 - z)^2, &amp; \tfrac{1}{2} &lt; z \le 1, \\
                       0, &amp; z &gt; 1, \end{cases}
  \qquad z = \frac{|r|}{a}.
\]</formula> <formula id="81">$ w $</formula> is the quadratic B-spline on the knots <formula id="84">$ \{-a, -a/2, a/2, a\} $</formula>, scaled to <formula id="85">$ w(0) = 1 $</formula>; it is <formula id="86">$ C^1 $</formula>-continuous, so the kernel and the resulting reproducing kernel shape functions are <formula id="86">$ C^1 $</formula>.</para>
<para>The support is the open box <formula id="87">$ |x_i - x_{A,i}| &lt; a $</formula>, <formula id="88">$ i = 1, \dots, d $</formula> (hence &quot;boxed&quot;); its bounding box is <formula id="89">$ [\boldsymbol{x}_A - a, \boldsymbol{x}_A + a] $</formula>. The support radius <formula id="61">$ a $</formula> is the half edge length of the box, identical in all directions, and the kernel is not normalized (the reproducing kernel correction removes any constant scaling of the kernel).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>The kernel does not own its center coordinates: it stores the pointer passed to the constructor, and <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_kernel_function_b_spline2nd_order_boxed_1a33aa45f04c0f1d38a74d101efb434bd0" kindref="member">moveTo()</ref> writes the new center through this pointer. The pointed-to storage must outlive the kernel. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
